<title>USA: Palm Beach Cty, Fla., repriced, top yield raised.</title>
<headline>Palm Beach Cty, Fla., repriced, top yield raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bear Stearns &amp; Co said Monday it repriced Palm Beach County, Fla.'s $28 million bond issue, raising the top yield in 2016 to 5.60 percent from 5.55 percent.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:</p>
<p>PALM BEACH COUNTY, FLORIDA</p>
<p>RE: $28,005,000*</p>
<p>STADIUM FACILITIES REVENUE BONDS</p>
<p>SERIES 1996</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>THERE ARE BALANCES 2008 THROUGH 2010.</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Aaa - MBIA	S&amp;P: AAA - MBIA</p>
<p>    DATED: 12/01/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 06/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 12/01</p>
<p> MATURITY		AMOUNT*    COUPON	   PRICE</p>
<p>12/01/1997		  880M    3.65  %	100.00</p>
<p>12/01/1998		  920M    3.95  %	100.00</p>
<p>12/01/1999		  955M    4.10  %	  4.15</p>
<p>12/01/2000		  995M    4.25  %	  4.30</p>
<p>12/01/2001		1,035M    4.40  %	  4.45</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>12/01/2002		1,085M    4.50  %	  4.55</p>
<p>12/01/2003		1,130M    4.60  %	  4.65</p>
<p>12/01/2004		1,185M    4.70  %	  4.75</p>
<p>12/01/2005		1,240M    4.80  %	  4.85</p>
<p>12/01/2006		1,300M    4.90  %	  4.95</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>12/01/2007		1,365M    5.00  %	  5.05</p>
<p>12/01/2008		1,430M    5.10  %	  5.15</p>
<p>12/01/2009		1,505M    5.20  %	  5.25</p>
<p>12/01/2010		1,580M    5.25  %	  5.35</p>
<p>12/01/2016	     11,400M    5.25  %	  5.60</p>
<p>					  (Approx. $ Price 95.825)</p>
<p>CALL FEATURES: 12/01/2007    102.00</p>
<p>		   DTP 12/01/2009</p>
<p>* - APPROXIMATE SUBJECT TO CHANGE</p>
<p>The compliance addendum MSRB Rule G-11 will apply.</p>
<p>The award is expected on Tuesday, December 17, 1996.</p>
<p>Delivery is expected on December 30, 1996.</p>
<p>This issue is book entry through DTC.</p>
<p>Bear, Stearns &amp; Co. Inc.</p>
<p>PaineWebber Incorporated</p>
<p>LM Capital Securities, Inc.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
